# Build-context exclusions.
#
# The build context is the repository root, so anything not listed here is
# copied to the builder. Two categories matter: development state that must
# never reach an image (keys, ciphertext, logs) and bulk that would only slow
# the build. `docker build` refuses to include a path that .gitignore has, but
# it does not read .gitignore — hence this explicit list.

# ── Never ship these ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local development state: signing seed, KEK file, folders, daemon logs.
.dev/
# Any real environment file. Credentials are mounted at run time, not baked in.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.kek

# ── Version control and editor noise ─────────────────────────────────────────
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# ── Build output and dependencies ────────────────────────────────────────────
# node_modules must be excluded at every depth: the root copy alone would still
# transfer ~180MB from packages/*/node_modules and slow every build.
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
bin/
build/
.next/
out/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── Generated documentation and spec workspace ───────────────────────────────
.usm-workspace/
apps/*/.usm-workspace/
docs/.vitepress/cache/
docs/.vitepress/dist/
tests/auto-generated/

# ── Local test and tool artifacts ────────────────────────────────────────────
coverage/
.nyc_output/
# Python virtualenvs are large (~120MB each); exclude at every depth, or the
# build walks them even though they would not be copied.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/*.egg-info/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
*.test
*.log
